          "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
          "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be an additive functor\nbetween abelian categories and assume\n<MATH_0002> is everywhere defined.\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> The functors <MATH_0003>, <MATH_0004> come equipped with a canonical\nstructure of a <MATH_0005>-functor from <MATH_0006>, see\nHomology, Definition <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0004> If every object of <MATH_0007> is a subobject of a right\nacyclic object for <MATH_0008>, then <MATH_0009> is a\nuniversal <MATH_0010>-functor, see\nHomology, Definition <REF_0002>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n<STRUCT_0006>",
          "source_status": "CURRENT",
          "placeholders": {
            "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}",
            "LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-right-derived-delta-functor}",
            "MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B}$",
            "MATH_0002": "$RF : D^{+}(\\mathcal{A}) \\to D^{+}(\\mathcal{B})$",
            "STRUCT_0002": "\\begin{enumerate}",
            "STRUCT_0003": "\\item",
            "MATH_0003": "$R^iF$",
            "MATH_0004": "$i \\geq 0$",
            "MATH_0005": "$\\delta$",
            "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B}$",
            "REF_0001": "\\ref{homology-definition-cohomological-delta-functor}",
            "STRUCT_0004": "\\item",
            "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{A}$",
            "MATH_0008": "$F$",
            "MATH_0009": "$\\{R^iF, \\delta\\}_{i \\geq 0}$",
            "MATH_0010": "$\\delta$",
            "REF_0002": "\\ref{homology-definition-universal-delta-functor}",
            "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}",
            "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{lemma}"
          },
