          "node_kind": "definition",
          "risk_level": "R3",
          "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14",
          "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a topological group.\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> A <TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0002>-module<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, sometimes called a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>discrete <MATH_0003>-module<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>,\nis an abelian group <MATH_0004> endowed with a left action <MATH_0005>\nby group homomorphisms such that <MATH_0006> is continuous when <MATH_0007> is given the\ndiscrete topology.\n<STRUCT_0004> A <TEXTITOPEN_0003>morphism of <MATH_0008>-modules<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> <MATH_0009> is a\n<MATH_0010>-equivariant homomorphism from <MATH_0011> to <MATH_0012>.\n<STRUCT_0005> The category of <MATH_0013>-modules is denoted <MATH_0014>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nLet <MATH_0015> be a ring.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n<STRUCT_0008> An <TEXTITOPEN_0004><MATH_0016>-module<TEXTITCLOSE_0004> is an <MATH_0017>-module <MATH_0018> endowed with\na left action <MATH_0019> by <MATH_0020>-linear maps such that <MATH_0021>\nis continuous when <MATH_0022> is given the discrete topology.\n<STRUCT_0009> A <TEXTITOPEN_0005>morphism of <MATH_0023>-modules<TEXTITCLOSE_0005> <MATH_0024> is a\n<MATH_0025>-equivariant <MATH_0026>-module map from <MATH_0027> to <MATH_0028>.\n<STRUCT_0010> The category of <MATH_0029>-modules is denoted <MATH_0030>.\n<STRUCT_0011>\n<STRUCT_0012>",
          "source_status": "CURRENT",
